      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 26. संयमः—restraint over the mind ( i. e. checking such",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "a desire ). काले—at the proper time, timely ( charity ). शक्त्या—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "i. e. यथाशक्ति according to one's power or means. युवति०—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "maintaining silence with regard to speaking about other",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "peoples' wives; in such cases जन means ‘a collection.’ परेषां—is.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "connected with युवति० by सापेक्षत्वेपि गमकत्वात् ( when the connec-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "tion is easily understood ) समासः । For a similar idea cf,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "अनिर्वर्णनीयं परकलत्रं नाम । S'ak. V. युवति is the fem. of युवन्, Pán.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "IV. 1. 77. तृष्णास्रोतः—The idea recurs in Vai. S'a. sl. 45. ( आशा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "नाम नदी &c. ). सामान्यः—सह मानेन वर्तते समानः । ततः स्वार्थे ष्यञ् । See",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "Vârt. on Pán. V. 1. 124. Common to all the S'ástras. अनुपहत०—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "whose application (operation) is unobstructed i. e. which never",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "fails to produce the desired effect. ‘Which violates no rules or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "ordinances.’ K. T. Telang. श्रेयसां—Blessìngs of all kinds.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 27. नीचैः—by low or poor-spirited men, men incapable of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "sustained exertion. निकृष्टाम् ईं शोभां चिनोतीति; नि + ई + चि + डः ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "मध्याः—men of the 2nd class. Cf. Mudràrákshasa Act. II. 70.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 28. प्रिया—Agreeable and yet not departing from, stand-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ing to, justice, just. वृत्तिः—course of conduct, behaviour. मलिन—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "मलोऽस्यास्ति । मल् + इनच् अस्त्यर्थे । see Pân. V. 2. 114. A dirty or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "foul deed. असन्तः &c.—Because अनिष्टादिष्टलाभेपि न गतिर्जायते शुभा ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "सुहृद्—For deri. see supra. 21. Mr. Joglekar takes this in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "general sense of ‘ a noble minded person, ’ deriving it as शोभनं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "हृत् यस्य, as oppossed to असन्तः. But I am inclined to take it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "rather in its restricted sense of ‘ a friend ’ who alone may be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "appealed to for help under any circumstances, and not every",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "good person. The force of अपि is then properly brought out.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "The use of the sing. सुहृद् also shows that that is the intention of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "the poet. Otherwise he should have used the plural correspond-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "ing to सन्तः. उच्चैः स्थेयम्—Acting nobly, keeping up one’s dignity.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "Cf. S'is. IX. 5. पदमनुविधेयं &c.—Tread, follow, in the foot-steps",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "( of the great ). उद्दिष्ट—is here used for उपदिष्ट advised, dictated.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "असिधाराव्रतम्—Three meanings can be assigned to this:—( 1 )",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
